---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Frequently Asked Questions | bestfinancecalculator.com"
  description="Find answers to common questions about our mortgage and loan calculators, data privacy, and mathematical accuracy."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold font-display tracking-tight text-main-text">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-text">
        Everything you need to know about our calculators, formulas, and privacy standards.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 space-y-8">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Is my financial data saved or shared?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-text leading-relaxed">
          No. We operate on a privacy-first model. All calculations are performed entirely client-side using JavaScript in your web browser. None of the values you type into the calculators are ever sent to our servers or shared with third parties.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          How accurate are the mortgage calculations?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-text leading-relaxed">
          Our calculator uses standard monthly amortization formulas that are widely accepted by financial institutions in the US, Canada, UK, and Australia. While our mathematical model is highly precise, actual loan terms depend on your lender's policies, credit history, compounding frequency, and escrow setups.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          How do extra monthly payments affect my mortgage?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-text leading-relaxed">
          Adding an extra monthly payment directly reduces your outstanding principal balance. Because interest is calculated on the remaining balance, paying extra shortens your loan term and saves you significant interest expenses over the lifetime of the loan.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Why are repayment frequencies important for personal loans?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-text leading-relaxed">
          Making weekly or fortnightly repayments rather than monthly payments means you pay down the loan balance faster. Over time, this decreases the interest compounding periods, allowing you to pay off your personal loan sooner and pay less total interest.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Is bestfinancecalculator.com free to use?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-text leading-relaxed">
          Yes, our financial tools are 100% free, require no registration, have no advertising, and collect no personal data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
